e retrieved from the archives of the Department of Pathology, Leuven Catholic University. Tumor classification was done by an experienced soft tissue pathologist (R. S.), using the criteria for DF in the WHO classification.^{8} Immunostainings were performed as described.^{3} Data concerning patient sex and age, tumor location, depth and size and karyotype are shown in Table 1.\n\nTable 1 Clinical and cytogenetic information\n\n### Cytogenetic Analysis\n\nAll cases were analyzed by chromosome banding after short-term culturing according to standard methods. Karyotypes were described according the International System for Human Cytogenetic Nomenclature.^{9}\n\n### FISH Analysis\n\nFISH was performed in four cases (cases 1 and 4–6). To pinpoint the breakpoint at 11q12, bacterial artificial chromosome (BAC) and fosmid probes spanning the breakpoint region were used (Table 2). --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n(PDF) Characterization of the human CREB3L2 gene promoter (https://www.researchgate.net/publication/24003663_Characterization_of_the_human_CREB3L2_gene_promoter)\nciteturn55search8 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 months ago; activation was consistently seen for the FUS/CREB3L2 ... CREB3L2 and FUS/CREB3L2 were localized to reticular ... Materials and methods ... reaction volume containing 1X AccuPrime Pfx reaction mix,\nthe first 120 amino acids (aa). Much stronger transcriptional\n\nactivation was consistently seen for the FUS/CREB3L2\n\nconstructs, in which the first 224 aa of CREB3L2 are replaced\n\nby the first 212 aa of FUS, than for the corresponding\n\nCREB3L2 constructs. Transcriptional activity was achieved\n\nthrough the box-B element, ATF6 and CRE binding sites, as\n\nwell as the GRP78 promoter. Proteins encoded by full-length\n\nCREB3L2 and FUS/CREB3L2 were localized to reticular\n\nstructures of the cytoplasm, whereas the corresponding,\n\ntruncated proteins lacking the transmembrane domain and the\n\ncarbox